  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promotion of Accountability, Civic Engagement and Rights</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Programme will operate with three intervention areas: strengthening accountability, enhancing civic engagement, and promoting and protecting rights. Outcome objectives and indicators are defined for each intervention area. The Programme will support relevant studies and research to sustain the activities under each intervention area. The Programme will work with civil society partners selected through calls for proposals and may work with building capacity in selected government institutions. The Programme will be managed by the Royal Danish Embassy in Kampala, responsible for the management of funds from other development partners on principles of delegated partnership. The Programme will run from 2023 to 2027 with an overall budget of DKK 300 million of which DKK 75 million are from Denmark.The Programme will mainly be driven by civil society organizations.  The civil society partners will be selected through a process of calls for proposals. The proposed projects&#x2019; relevance and contribution to overall Programme objectives, as well as the partner organization&#x2019;s capacity to implement will guide the selection. The programme may also work with selected government institutions (duty bearers) directly or through partners. Before engaging in direct or indirect funding of government institutions the Danish Embassy will carry out a thorough political economy analysis of the selected institution.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To strengthen democratic values, protection of human rights and civic space</narrative>
  </description>
